msgid "The only lane in this subprocess, so nothing produced here is checked by a different party before it reaches the L1 graph. Two of these eight tasks (Task_Archive, Task_TechMeta) still say NOT IMPLEMENTED; Task_Provenance's citation of who or what wrote each narrative is what is meant to stand between a generated description and its being treated as source material."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-derive-content.bpmn:125
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The pdf-footnotes.py arm (owner, 2026-11-11, \"also foot notes/marks\"): from the page layout, each note at the foot of a page and every superscript mark in the text that calls it, written to footnotes.json (folio-document-footnotes/v1) with the block that holds the page. The section text is not changed. Only a called note is a footnote; uncalled foot-of-page lines and marks with no note are listed, never dropped. OCR'd pages have no fonts and are reported unread. Method: skill l1-document-ingestion, \"Footnotes and their marks\"."
msgstr ""

#: ../folio-assistant-core/processes/library/ingest-derive-content.bpmn:116
#. Diagram element documentation
msgid "The pdf-images.py, pdf-vector-labels.py and pdf-vector-figures.py arms extract the raster images and the figures drawn as vectors (grouped and rendered). For every table the document's structure declares, an agent reads the rendered page, checks cell text against the text layer, and writes tables/<label>.csv plus tables.csvw.json (folio-tabular-csvw/v1), with a draft description in the six UN languages; pdf-tables.py's grid is a cross-check, not the answer. Owner, 2026-11-11 (who-iris): \"actually extract the figures\" and \"any tables too\". Method: skill document-intake, \"Figures and captioned tables: describe, keep, transcribe\"."
msgstr ""

